#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276625 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5000a4b1-c0cb-59f3-9d45-6287fa8ac9b6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Using the Law of Total Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e681789e-3820-5435-931b-c670b05d4f20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276627} {:answer/id #uuid "b7bc353b-6624-5b5a-99d9-a9600220dbd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276628} {:answer/id #uuid "bd9e3ba9-2b23-51f6-8488-d645a921511f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276629} {:answer/id #uuid "075313a6-b9e6-5009-bf30-c56820ee6d26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276630} {:answer/id #uuid "4edcca36-1fdc-5214-964a-9b8525f3147a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4edcca36-1fdc-5214-964a-9b8525f3147a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276631} :answer-field/id #uuid "c37260f1-3b1b-529a-ab93-395ac44e8e24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "04972e8d-97c8-5950-88bf-255659e0f8d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-122398" :question/problem "There are two bags in a box, $A$ and $B.$ In bag $A,$ there are $7$ red marbles and $3$ green marbles. We choose a bag at random with a probability of $\\frac{1}{2}$ each, and then we pick a marble from the chosen bag. The probability that the result of this experiment is a green marble is $\\frac{1}{2}.$ What is the probability that a randomly selected marble from bag $B$ is green?" :question/worked-solution "Let $G$ be the event that a green marble is selected, and let $A$ be the event that bag $A$ is selected. Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that bag $B$ is selected. \n\nTo calculate the probability that a selected marble is green, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(G)=P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since there are $2$ bags, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=\\frac{1}{2},\\,P({A}^{′})=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n- Since there are $3$ green marbles of the total of $10$ marbles in bag $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(G|A)=\\frac{3}{10}.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected marble in both bags is green is $\\frac{1}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nP(G)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(G|{A}^{′}),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =(\\frac{3}{10})(\\frac{1}{2})+P(G|{A}^{′})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{3}{20}+\\frac{1}{2}P(G|{A}^{′}) \\\\ 20\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) & =20\\cdot (\\frac{3}{20}+\\frac{1}{2}P(G|{A}^{′}))​ \\\\ 10 & =3+10P(G|{A}^{′}) \\\\ 7 & =10P(G|{A}^{′}) \\\\ P(G|{A}^{′}) & =\\frac{7}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected marble from bag $B$ is green is $\\frac{7}{10}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083868 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5000a4b1-c0cb-59f3-9d45-6287fa8ac9b6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Using the Law of Total Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a179dfeb-c4c1-506a-999c-5013918b3446" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{120}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082575} {:answer/id #uuid "02d0e297-baeb-59fc-addc-5d5bedde02d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082576} {:answer/id #uuid "33b923fc-72c0-5f7c-9e58-6911b395fbf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082577} {:answer/id #uuid "55c40263-1a95-5cf5-9e83-95a0d94e50c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082578} {:answer/id #uuid "71bbd0ce-edad-52e4-aae3-8e02b2385397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02d0e297-baeb-59fc-addc-5d5bedde02d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082576} :answer-field/id #uuid "5297d0f9-8b16-5287-8b4a-e7f4cc3a3754" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dfc184b2-405b-5616-ae5a-9b803be06566" :question/math-academy-id "q-88581" :question/problem "In a class, $\\frac{3}{5}$ of the students are boys, and $\\frac{2}{5}$ are girls. Of the boys, $\\frac{1}{12}$ of them play basketball. The probability that a randomly selected student plays basketball is $\\frac{1}{15}.$ If a girl is selected at random, what is the probability that she plays basketball?" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the event that the chosen student plays basketball, and let $B$ be the event that the student is a boy. Then ${B}^{′}$ is the event that the student is a girl.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected student plays basketball, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(A)=P(A|B)P(B)+P(A|{B}^{′})P({B}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $\\frac{3}{5}$ of the students are boys and $\\frac{2}{5}$ are girls, we have\n\n$$\nP(B)=\\frac{3}{5},\\,P({B}^{′})=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{1}{12}$ of the boys play basketball, we have\n\n$$\nP(A|B)=\\frac{1}{12}.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected student plays basketball is $\\frac{1}{15},$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=\\frac{1}{15}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(A|{B}^{′}),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A) & =P(A|B)P(B)+P(A|{B}^{′})P({B}^{′}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{15} & =(\\frac{1}{12})(\\frac{3}{5})+P(A|{B}^{′})(\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{15} & =\\frac{1}{20}+\\frac{2}{5}P(A|{B}^{′}) \\\\ 60\\cdot (\\frac{1}{15}) & =60\\cdot (\\frac{1}{20}+\\frac{2}{5}P(A|{B}^{′}))​ \\\\ 4 & =3+24P(A|{B}^{′}) \\\\ 1 & =24P(A|{B}^{′}) \\\\ P(A|{B}^{′}) & =\\frac{1}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected girl plays basketball is $\\frac{1}{24}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276632 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f7055d-9f45-5115-97f4-35d0c56008e0" :knowledge-point/title "Using The Law of Total Probability Stated in Terms of Conditional Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "838eb887-1519-5976-9ca3-e9ceb7fe26ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.035" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276634} {:answer/id #uuid "5e779bcb-5e73-5939-adaf-021ff452d72f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.110" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276635} {:answer/id #uuid "208ca91f-e4be-5586-9214-c70642d6e813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.085" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276636} {:answer/id #uuid "ad02b946-cea5-542c-88ef-aa44450337ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276637} {:answer/id #uuid "17e959ef-237e-52b1-bd5c-b96e4822c45e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.058" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17e959ef-237e-52b1-bd5c-b96e4822c45e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.058" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276638} :answer-field/id #uuid "95ce6563-e92a-5e44-a0fb-6660178cb6f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ad4daafd-68e2-51a2-8ef4-2f5861f8fe15" :question/math-academy-id "q-88978" :question/problem "A company manufactures electronic components. Of the components manufactured, $45%$ are produced by machine $A$, and the remaining $55%$ are produced by machine $B.$ If $8%$ of the components produced by machine $A$ are defective and $4%$ of the components produced by machine $B$ are defective, what is the probability that a randomly selected component is defective?" :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that the selected component is defective, and let $A$ be the event that the component was produced by machine $A.$ Then, ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the component was produced by machine $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected component is defective, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(D)=P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since machine $A$ produces $45%$ of the components and $B$ the remaining $55%$, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.45,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.55.\n$$\n\n- Since $8%$ of the components produced by machine $A$ are defective, and $4%$ of the components produced by machine $B$ are defective, we have\n\n$$\nP(D|A)=0.08,\\,P(D|{A}^{′})=0.04.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected component is defective is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\  & =(0.08)(0.45)+(0.04)(0.55) \\\\  & =0.058.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276639 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f7055d-9f45-5115-97f4-35d0c56008e0" :knowledge-point/title "Using The Law of Total Probability Stated in Terms of Conditional Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f773d584-3da5-5501-a535-33dbefa74e23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276641} {:answer/id #uuid "4c02db2f-3276-5e84-9bdb-252f90ae30af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276642} {:answer/id #uuid "a91999a4-f8bc-5ab2-811d-cfe96d94f174" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276643} {:answer/id #uuid "3efaddb0-802d-515b-b41d-9a7880bcca36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276644} {:answer/id #uuid "2a0ef903-3313-5fed-90c7-c57ee172d064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f773d584-3da5-5501-a535-33dbefa74e23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276641} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2f4b2c8-a428-5336-8561-3ead83a8ae75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276640}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "58a06f5c-02d5-5e7d-a909-7ddd7de0f5df" :question/math-academy-id "q-89034" :question/problem "Robert has a desk with two drawers, drawer $A$ and drawer $B.$ Of the pens in his drawers, $\\frac{4}{5}$ of them are in drawer $A,$ and $\\frac{1}{5}$ are in drawer $B.$ Among the pens in drawer $A,$ $\\frac{1}{3}$ of them are blue and, of the pens in drawer $B,$ $\\frac{1}{6}$ of them are blue. What is the probability that a randomly selected pen is blue?" :question/worked-solution "Let $U$ be the event that the chosen pen is blue, and let $A$ be the event that the pen was selected from drawer $A.$ Then, ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the pen was selected from drawer $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected pen is blue, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(U)=P(U|A)P(A)+P(U|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $\\frac{4}{5}$ of the pens are in drawer $A$ and $\\frac{1}{5}$ are in drawer $B$, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=\\frac{4}{5},\\,P({A}^{′})=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the pens in drawer $A$ are blue and $\\frac{1}{6}$ of the pens in drawer $B$ are blue, we have\n\n$$\nP(U|A)=\\frac{1}{3},\\,P(U|{A}^{′})=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected pen is blue is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(U) & =P(U|A)P(A)+P(U|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3})(\\frac{4}{5})+(\\frac{1}{6})(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{15}+\\frac{1}{30} \\\\  & =\\frac{8+1}{30} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5000a4b1-c0cb-59f3-9d45-6287fa8ac9b6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Using the Law of Total Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a79bcdd9-177c-5ae8-b0af-d47ddd1b2915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276648} {:answer/id #uuid "3614afd4-e630-530c-9829-a3c343dab03f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276649} {:answer/id #uuid "ad229534-bf18-5b9d-beac-9197500c5fc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276650} {:answer/id #uuid "3e20358a-71b8-5165-8022-95eb8e228390" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276651} {:answer/id #uuid "5f594f04-0522-565a-87a5-447ee5be0aec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f594f04-0522-565a-87a5-447ee5be0aec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276652} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7006d1b-ed94-56f7-a623-337c4799da3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276647}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c27c3aea-7db0-557e-90fa-11207673f0db" :question/math-academy-id "q-89043" :question/problem "A student sits a multiple-choice test. Each question on the test has $n$ possible answers, and only one choice is correct. The student knows the correct answer to $70%$ of the questions. If the student decides to select an answer at random for the questions that they do not know, and the probability that a randomly selected question from the test is answered correctly is $0.76,$ what is the value of $n?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be the event that a randomly selected question is correct, and let $K$ be the event that the student knows the answer. Then ${K}^{′}$ is the event that the student doesn't know the answer.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected question is correct, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(C)=P(C|K)P(K)+P(C|{K}^{′})P({K}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since the student knows the answer to $70%$ of the questions, we have\n\n$$\nP(K)=0.7,\\,P({K}^{′})=0.3.\n$$\n\n- Since each question has $n$ possible answers, we have\n\n$$\nP(C|K)=1,\\,P(C|{K}^{′})=\\frac{1}{n}.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected question is answered correctly is $0.76,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(C)=0.76.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $n,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C|K)P(K)+P(C|{K}^{′})P({K}^{′}) \\\\ 0.76 & =(1)(0.70)+(\\frac{1}{n})(0.3) \\\\ 0.76 & =0.70+\\frac{0.3}{n} \\\\ \\frac{0.3}{n} & =0.06 \\\\ n & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the test has $5$ possible answers for each question."}]}
